<title>USA: Lockheed Martin wins contract increase.</title>
<headline>Lockheed Martin wins contract increase.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Air Force said Wednesday it had awarded a $118 million contract increase to Lockheed Martin Corp for four C-130H troop-carrying planes for Taiwan.</p>
<p>It said the contract involves unique modification of the planes for Taiwan. Other countries must buy such major weapons from the U.S. military, not directly from U.S. contractors.</p>
</text>
